    {
      "field": "applicant_2.employment",
      "needed_for": ["updating_employment_income_details"],
      "follow_up_question": "What is Sara's current employment status and monthly income?"
    }
  ],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "The HFE letter is valid for 9 months, not a year, and you should apply now if you meet the eligibility criteria, but eligibility for engaged couples is unconfirmed.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "An HFE letter stays valid for 9 months, counted from the date HDB issues it.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HFE-VALID-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Eligibility of engaged couples for the first‑timer (FT) category is not stated in the official criteria; HDB has not confirmed that engaged couples can qualify.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Apply for the HFE letter online via the HDB Flat Portal with Singpass as soon as you are ready, because the application is free and the letter is needed before you can submit a flat application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HFE-APPLY-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "If you obtain the HFE letter now, it will expire 9 months later, which may be before the October launch you are targeting; you would need to re‑apply for a new HFE letter before the flat application deadline.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [
    {
      "field": "relationship",
      "needed_for": ["eligibility_assessment"],
      "follow_up_question": "Can you confirm whether you are married or still engaged at the time of applying for the HFE letter?"
    }
  ],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "You do not need to register your marriage before applying for a BTO; the marriage must be registered within 3 months after the flat purchase is completed.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "text": "An engaged couple can apply for a BTO without having registered their marriage first.",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "text": "The marriage must be registered no later than 3 months after the flat purchase is completed, and HDB may ask to see the marriage certificate.",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HH-MARRY-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "text": "Prepare to register your marriage within the 3‑month window after you receive the key for your new flat.",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "As an engaged Singapore‑Citizen couple with no prior flat ownership, you must first confirm eligibility (engaged couples are not confirmed under the first‑timer rules), obtain an HFE letter, and then prepare the required documents and steps for a BTO application.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "First‑timer couples are defined as married couples aged 40 or below; the eligibility of engaged couples is unconfirmed.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["PRI-FTPMC-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Both applicants must be Singapore Citizens for a new flat under the couples scheme.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HH-CIT-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Applicants must never have owned or sold a residential property, including any HDB flat, and must not have booked a BTO or SBF flat in the past 5 years.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["PRI-FTPMC-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c4",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Check whether you can apply as an engaged couple via the fiancé/fiancée scheme; if not, you would need to be married before applying.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c5",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Apply for an HFE (Housing Flat Eligibility) letter on the HDB Flat Portal before the BTO ballot opens.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c6",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Gather the documents required for the HFE application: NRICs, proof of Singapore citizenship, employment letters, latest payslips, and a declaration of no prior flat ownership.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c7",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "The exact list of documents for the HFE letter may change; please verify the current checklist on the HDB website.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c8",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "If you have a child (Singapore Citizen or SPR) or are expecting a child, obtain the relevant birth certificate or doctor's certification, as this affects eligibility under the FT(PMC) criteria.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["PRI-FTPMC-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c9",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "Once the HFE letter is issued, keep it valid (it is typically valid for 6 months) and note its expiry date; if it will expire within 30 days before you need to submit a flat application, request a fresh letter as per HFE renewal rules.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HFE-RENEW-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c10",
      "kind": "preparation_step",
      "text": "When the BTO ballot opens, log in to the HDB Flat Portal, select your preferred project and flat type, and submit the application before the deadline.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c11",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Specific ballot dates, flat types available to engaged couples, and any priority schemes (e.g., FCS) should be checked on the HDB portal for the current BTO launch.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [
    {
      "field": "children_or_expecting",
      "needed_for": ["eligibility_assessment", "HFE_letter_requirements"],
      "follow_up_question": "Do you currently have a Singapore Citizen or Permanent Resident child, or are you expecting a child?"
    },
    {
      "field": "hfe_status",
      "needed_for": ["application_timeline"],
      "follow_up_question": "Have you already applied for or received an HFE letter?"
    }
  ],
  "profile_conflicts": [],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "The FT(PMC) category requires that neither applicant has ever owned or sold a residential property, so Darren’s prior HDB flat disqualifies the couple from using FT(PMC).",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "FT(PMC) families must never have owned or sold a residential property, including an HDB flat.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["PRI-FTPMC-001"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c2",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "Buyers do not apply for the FT(PMC) category; HDB determines eligibility after the flat application is submitted.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["PRI-FTPMC-002"]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "c3",
      "kind": "caveat",
      "text": "Because Darren previously owned and sold an HDB flat, the couple does not meet the FT(PMC) eligibility condition; you should consider applying under the regular first‑timer (couples) scheme instead.",
      "cited_fact_ids": []
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
  "profile_conflicts": [
    {
      "fields": ["applicant_1.prior_flat_or_subsidy"],
      "kind": "logical_inconsistency",
      "detail": "The situation states both are first‑timers, but also says Darren bought and sold an HDB flat in the past, which conflicts with the FT(PMC) requirement of never having owned or sold a residential property.",
      "quotes": [
        "We're both first-timers.",
        "Before we met, Darren (35) bought a flat from HDB with his ex-wife; he sold it in 2020."
      ],
      "clarification_question": "Do you still wish to apply under the regular first‑timer couples scheme rather than FT(PMC) given Darren’s prior flat ownership?"
    }
  ],
  "out_of_scope_reasons": []
}

{
  "summary": "Yes, both of you can be applicants as you are Singapore Citizens, first‑timers, and both over 21 years old.",
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "c1",
      "kind": "policy_fact",
      "text": "If both partners in an engaged couple are Singapore Citizens and are over 21 years old, each can appear as an applicant in the BTO application.",
      "cited_fact_ids": ["HH-AGE-002"]
    }
  ],
  "missing_profile_fields": [],
